cff-version: 1.2.0
title: SymbolicUncertainties.jl
message: >-
  If you use this software in work that leads to a publication, please
  cite it. The licence does not require this — no OSI-approved licence
  can — but citation is how scientific software stays maintained.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Celles
    given-names: Sébastien
    email: s.celles@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/s-celles/SymbolicUncertainties.jl
url: https://s-celles.github.io/SymbolicUncertainties.jl/
abstract: >-
  Purely symbolic propagation of measurement uncertainties following
  JCGM 100:2008 (GUM). Quantities carry the independent sources they
  derive from, so combined uncertainties, sensitivity coefficients,
  budgets and covariances are all derived from one structure, and
  correlation between quantities sharing an upstream measurement is
  propagated without a user-supplied covariance matrix.
keywords:
  - uncertainty propagation
  - metrology
  - GUM
  - JCGM 100:2008
  - symbolic computation
  - measurement uncertainty
  - Julia
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 0.10.0
